{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (86.36%) to hepcidin TH1-5 C: 38%. Activity: active against Gram- S. flexneri (MIC 3-6 uM), P. fluorescens (MIC 6-12 uM), P. stutzeri (MIC 1.5-3 um), E. coli QZ18109 or QZ18110 (MIC 3-12 uM), P. aeruginosa QZ19124 or QZ19125 (MIC 6-12 uM), A. baumannii QZ18050A or QZ18055 (MIC 1.5-3 uM), K. pneumoniae QZ18106 or QZ18107 (MIC 6-24 uM), A. hydrophila (MIC 24-48 uM), E. tarda (MIC 24-48 uM), A. sobria (MIC 24-48 uM), Gram+ S. epidermidis (MIC 6-12 uM), C. glutamicum (MIC 3-6 uM), B. subtilis (MIC 6-12 uM), E. faecium QZ18080 (MIC 6-12 uM) and fungi C. neoformans (MIC 12-24 uM). Recombinant production:yeast:Pichia pastoris: recombinant peptide rLJ-hep2 and syntehtic form were obtained for additional stuides ( Gong et al., 2022). Update 7/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36286474", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mar Drugs. 2022 Oct 20;20(10):651. doi: 10.3390/md20100651. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04046", "source_id": "AP04046", "source_numeric_id": "04046", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04046", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The Antimicrobial Peptide LJ-hep2 from Lateolabrax japonicus Exerting Activities against Multiple Pathogenic Bacteria and Immune Protection In Vivo", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
